  <participating-org role="4" type="90">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ONG Actions de d&#xe9;veloppement et de</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The NGO Actions de d&#xe9;veloppement et de protection de l&apos;Enfant pour une citoyennet&#xe9; Responsable (AER) is a non-governmental and non-profit organization (NGO) focused on children, youth and development actions. It was founded in 2004 in Niamey under the name Assistance aux Enfants de la Rue.
The transition from Assistance to Street Children to the new name &quot;Actions for the development-protection of Responsible Child-Citizenship&quot; is motivated by the simple fact that the NGO must be part of the new so-called systemic or holistic approach adopted by the Government through the Framework Document of the Child Protection Policy in 2014. Previous interventionsby the NGO AER were carried out under the categorical approach of focusing on the child or a category of children without taking into account their environment. While the systemic approach focuses on the child&apos;s environment, the family environment, in short, calls on several actors to provide adequate responses to the problems experienced by the child at various levels. The mission of the NGOAER is to contribute to the promotion of the culture of responsible citizenship in general and in particular to the improvement of the living conditions of children and young people in vulnerable situations, which reinforces it in this action which aims to achieve results (Strengthening citizenship and democratic values as well as respect for human rights and preventing and resolving local conflicts in a non-violent way) by focusing on category 1.
Thus, the NGO AER pursues the following objectives:
General objective: To contribute to the improvement of the living conditions of communities and children and young people in vulnerable situations.
Specific objectives :
Promote an environment that protects children andyoung people and is conducive to their development;
To mobilize social assistance for the benefit of poor families with children in their care;
To promote the culture of responsible citizenship and non-violence;
To promote the integration of communities in the process of local and national development.</narrative>
